  - name: BPSA Excessive Queue Length
    detail: The BPSA MQ Queue has more than 10000 outstanding messages exceeding the alert threshold
    fluxfile: flux/bpsa_queue_length.flux
    severity: 1
    threshold: 10000
    comparison: ge
    tags: 
      - host
      - _field
      - _measurement
      - queue
    interval: 120
    target: xapi
    action: | 
              A large number of outstanding messages indicates that either the number of incoming messages is exceptionally large
              or there is a significant problem with processing. Use the Azure Portal Dashboard for BPSA to compare incoming
              message rates with outgoing. Unless there is exception volume (RRSP season) it is most likely the loss of a WLS 
              or a problem with database performnce. Ensure the WLS managed servers are healthy and engage a DBA to look at 
              Oracle stats.